 ### Min/Max Altitude Heightmap Optimization
-Stores per-column minimum and maximum occupied voxel heights to skip empty or fully occupied columns during meshing [S3, unofficial]. On voxel addition (index > 0), `OnVoxelAdded(i, j, k)` updates the heightmaps to reflect the new occupied column [S3, unofficial]. On voxel removal (index == 0), `OnVoxelRemoved(i, j, k)` updates the heightmaps to reflect the cleared column [S3, unofficial]. The `minAltitude` array is a byte array of size $ChunkSize^2$ (1024 bytes for $ChunkSize=32$), storing the lowest occupied Y index per XZ column [S3, unofficial]. The `maxAltitude` array is similarly sized, storing the highest occupied Y index [S3, unofficial]. Initialization sets `minAltitude` to $ChunkSize$ for all columns, indicating initially empty columns [S3, unofficial].
